      "description": "Parks Data Center Cachoeirinha, located in Cachoeirinha, Brazil, is a Tier III facility developed by Parks S/A Comunicações Digitais. The project involves an investment of R$ 500 million and is designed to meet the growing demand for data storage and processing, cloud computing, Artificial Intelligence (AI) applications, and critical digital services.\n\nThe facility will be developed in eight gradual and scalable expansion phases. The initial stage features 14 racks and marks the commencement of operations. The data center will have a total capacity of 5 MW and 3.3 MW of IT load, spread across two independent buildings, each containing four Data Halls. This configuration provides eight highly protected and isolated hosting environments. The Tier III certification ensures redundancy of critical systems, allowing for maintenance without operational interruption and a near-zero downtime index.\n\nThe investment aims to strengthen Brazil's digital infrastructure, offering a highly reliable environment for businesses and public entities to host their information securely, with high performance, and in compliance with Brazilian legislation. The facility is strategically positioned to address the need for increased capacity, resilience, and decentralization of digital infrastructure in Brazil, particularly in Rio Grande do Sul.",
